{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PRE-EMPTED A CLOSE-TIME BLOCKER. Checked attestation currency across all seven BEFORE trying to\nclose, rather than discovering it at close time:\n  87cb epic  stale-pin-drift  (I edited children after claiming it; the epic's review pins their\n                               material)\n  b0ac       stale-code       (its currency_basis is file_impact, and I later reworded\n                               src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py for the O_EXCL count — a file in its\n                               impact set, so the pinned blobs moved)\n  8ce5 f9b9 15f2 0880 9ca8    certified\nRebar enforces plan-review material pins on CLOSE as well as on start, so both would likely have\nrefused. Started fresh reviews for the two stale ones NOW, in parallel with the CI re-run, instead of\nserially afterwards — they are independent workloads and both take 15-20 min.\nGood moment for the epic's re-review: its children are final and will not be edited again, so the\npin it takes now should hold through the closes.\nAll seven are in_progress; the close sequence is blocked only on Verified +1 and these two\nattestations."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788330869214469001,"uuid":"7f9a5a68-3a93-4078-9912-fc79cdf84d21"}